WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:03.539
"Hmm, another rat."

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.980
"But those eyes."

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.774
"A starving wolf."

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.720
"Before I kill you

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.980
tell me your name. Tell me your name!

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.830
"No name to give. You shinobi are all the same."

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.980
"You die nameless with no one to mourn you."

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.720
"However, your left arm.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.029
"A prosthetic shinobi arm."

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:33.279
"It reminds me of..."

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:41.139
The reason he laughs is that once there was another with a similar name

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:44.493
Sekijo, the One-armed Orangutan.

00:00:44.493 --> 00:00:45.249
"It's it..."

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:47.899
"A one-armed wolf."

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.899
I like it, which means...

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.839
Sekiro. That is what I shall name you."

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.700
Words have meaning but names have power and

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.445
yours is tied to another.

00:00:59.445 --> 00:01:00.980
"I brought some sake."

00:01:00.985 --> 00:01:02.740
"Don't mind if I do."

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.460
"Is it not to your liking?"

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.820
"No, it's damn good."

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.893
"But it does make my old wounds ache."

00:01:17.893 --> 00:01:19.600
"Your left arm?"

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.999
"Yes, and this sake was the favorite

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.000
of the man who cut it off."

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:25.660
"Who was...?"

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.684
"Lord Isshin."

00:01:27.684 --> 00:01:28.860
"Isshin?"

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.300
"Why?"

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:39.790
"He did it for my sick. I was on the verge of being consumed."

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.060
"Consumed by what?"

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.700
"Shura."

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:51.910
"Well, whether you believe me or not that's for you to decide, but you do well to beware..."

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:54.350
"Shura's shadow."

00:01:54.350 --> 00:02:01.239
Shura is a sort of demon, a manifestation of hatred that can appear in those who kill excessively.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:02.840
Although,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.550
Isshin killed many, polishing his skills in the blood of his enemies

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.910
He did not succumb to Shura.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:09.970
Why?

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:14.949
Well, because after every enemy he killed he performed the Breath of Nature

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.759
expelling both regret and reaffirming his core.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:27.740
Shinobi, however, inherit the Karma of those they've killed and they become physically burdened with regrets as a result.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.480
"I see it in your eyes too."

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.220
"The shadow of Shura."

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:39.880
"Hmm, give me cause and I will kill you. You would do you well to remember that."

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.470
To understand what set the sculptor on his path to Shura

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:51.009
We look to his past, way back when he was still known as the Bounding Monkey of the Sunken Valley

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:57.130
"I trained in the techniques of the shinobi in the valley where the monkeys dwelled."
"By yourself?"

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:03.009
"No, there were two of us. We were rogue shinobi. There was no proper master for the likes of us."

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.870
"That's why we went to the valley. To run, to jump, to clash swords."

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:16.120
"Where one slip would mean your doom. That was how we trained. We came to move exactly as monkeys did after a time."

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.360
"I drink this monkey booze whenever I tired of training and I'd

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:27.600
listened to the howl of my partners whistling finger while I drank."

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.640
"How?"

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.700
"It was from that unique ring."

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:35.679
"Whistling through that ring would fill the valley with a somber melody."

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:41.499
"Strangely enough, I enjoyed that sound. I listened to it so often."

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:46.988
Her cry could once be heard all along the waterfront of the Sunken Valley as

00:03:47.299 --> 00:03:53.979
she whistled through this ring that could also send beasts wild and it was this same ring that was

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.760
unfortunately found in the belly of such a beast

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.500
and it's a sound that the sculptor will recall forever.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.200
"To think it was in the belly of an ape"

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:09.819
I'm sure it'll play a somber but enjoyable tune. Make sure you use it well."

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:17.260
Perhaps it was the loss of his training partner that set him on the path to Shura. After all, it's

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.260
implied that there was more between them. But after Isshin severed Shura's arm,

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:31.549
the flames of hatred receded and sculptor regained control. And after Sekijo's defeat, he's ties to the Ashina's deepened."

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.120
For Isshin had this charm about him.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:41.570
He had a way of turning his enemies into compatriots, especially those he respected for their battle prowess.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.977
For there were still many battles to be won.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:49.100
After one such battle, Sekijo found a young girl on the battlefield.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.780
She was staring up at him

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.940
so intently that he felt he had to give up this rice ball that he was eating.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.700
"When I was young

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.860
I stood alone in the aftermath of a battlefield. I was alone and

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.780
staring,

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.100
dumbfounded."

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:11.419
"I could do nothing, neither cry, nor even get angry"

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.240
"Complete shock and then there was a monkey eating a rice ball."

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:17.880
"A monkey?"

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.010
"Maybe an ape."

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:20.510
"Maybe."

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:26.689
"Either way, he made it look so delicious. I remember being angry at that but then,

00:05:27.539 --> 00:05:31.171
then he gave me the rice ball. It tasted so good."

00:05:31.171 --> 00:05:32.479
"What a kind monkey."

00:05:34.169 --> 00:05:35.750
"Yes"

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.500
"He was a very kind monkey."

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.880
After this Emma threw herself into medical work with her new mentor Dogen,

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.420
who was a doctor of incredible ability.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.230
"After that..."

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:53.980
well, a while later Ashina became a dangerous place for the both of us. Around then

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.010
Dogen adopted her as his daughter.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:05.410
I suppose it didn't really matter where she ended up. One thing's for sure: she's happier for the fact

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.319
she wasn't raised by a shinobi."

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:14.140
Our story is testament to that fact for we too were found on a battlefield by a shinobi.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:22.119
He was a cunning owl who would go on to use us to deny the self and to leave us nameless,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.120
save for being known as a loyal wolf.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:33.219
Yet we were saved once more in a sort of rebirth where our life became indebted to another, this time

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:37.329
not to a cunning owl but to a kind monkey instead,

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.860
and through him to the man who crafted his left arm.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.420
"About lady Emma's father..."

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.920
"Dogen. He was an extraordinary doctor."

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:53.880
"He was also very well versed in mechanisms and devices. Better put, he was obsessed with mechanisms

00:06:53.890 --> 00:07:00.489
to the point that it affected his health. He didn't take much else seriously, but I owed him my life."

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.359
"And we could say that you owe him your life as well."

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.520
"What do you mean?"

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.040
"When I lost my left arm

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.690
Dogen created that thing,

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:17.410
which has now become your left arm. The first version was a complete failure, it didn't work at all.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:23.380
So he remade it. Then he remade it again and again, countless times."

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:30.370
"What?" 
"He told me I needed to practice with the prosthetic in order to use it properly."

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:36.339
"So Emma would pester me into carving her spinning tops and other toys. After

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:44.220
much training of that sort it came to be called a shinobi fang. In other words, that

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.220
prosthetic arm

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.140
is Dogen's legacy."

00:07:48.149 --> 00:07:49.089
"His legacy?"

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.970
"So much time has passed."

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:58.720
"While I have abandoned my shinobi ways that alone I could not bear to abandon."

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:06.369
"I'd never have believed that one such as myself would save another who'd lost their arm like you have."

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.740
"I'm sure it is fate."

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.999
But all of these people, all of the Ashina lead back to Isshin

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.480
"There is something I'd like to ask you."
"Of course."

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:20.799
"Who trained you to fight with a blade?"
"A blade? I am a doctor."

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.010
"Yes, but who?"

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.540
"Lord Isshin."

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:35.049
"But I only have a passing interest."
"I did not believe your skill counts as a mere passing interest."

00:08:35.169 --> 00:08:37.040
"Why did you learn?"
"Well..."

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.600
"Not to kill people."
"What do you mean?"

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:44.500
"No, I don't have the slightest desire to kill anyone. It's just..."

00:08:45.889 --> 00:08:50.298
"I would want to kill a demon if one were to appear."
"A demon?!"

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:56.040
"Don't take me seriously. It was only a joke"

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:01.720
As Isshin would say, the bounds, the ties are so deeply amusing, and we are tied to Sekijo,

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.439
who is a constant warning of what a shinobi can become.

00:09:07.019 --> 00:09:10.758
Because once it's touched you Shura never really leaves

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:17.389
"War is on the horizon, a dreadful one. At that the Dead will rise as mountains and the hate

00:09:17.669 --> 00:09:22.279
will flow like an inferno. It will give birth to a demon."

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.760
"I'm certain of it."

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:29.120
The Interior Ministry tried and they failed to take Ashina once before.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:37.100
But now they're ready. They know its people they know their weaknesses. They know the land and this time they will set it ablaze.

00:09:38.309 --> 00:09:39.480
"Orangutan"

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:41.680
"The central forces are here."

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.940
"Are they now? They never change their thieving ways."

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.360
"Are the flames... still burning?"

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:53.520
"Emma, the answer to that isn't going to change. I could carve Buddha idols for all eternity,

00:09:53.680 --> 00:10:00.080
and the flames of hatred would still rage on. The most I can do is keep them in check."

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.280
"Orangutan..." 
"What is it?"

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.440
"If the time ever comes"

00:10:04.139 --> 00:10:06.130
then I'll..."

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.640
"I have ordered a carve. Goodbye."

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.180
"Listen..."
 "What?"

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:18.440
"You'll be the one to kill me."
"What are you talking about?"

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:22.180
"Don't play the fool to make her after kill me

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.220
I don't think I could bear it."

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.990
"Please..."

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:34.630
But if you don't have Kuro strength of purpose to guide you and if you kill for the sake of power like Owl does, then

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.000
we too can get lost.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.300
"No! Your..."

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.600
"You can't be Shura!"

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:57.740
But it doesn't have to be this way, for if you learn from the sculptors mistakes and fight for Kuro and not for hatred, then

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:02.259
you may become one who prevents Shura from taking root in the world.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:05.380
All it takes is to remember who we are.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.080
"Thank... you..."

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.180
"You know, don't you?"

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:24.040
"You know who the one-armed demon was before."

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.700
Yes

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:33.480
If you're like me and you find Sekiro's eastern philosophies fascinating, then

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:39.900
I'd like to put you onto this little audio book that I read last year and it's one that really changed the way I experience

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:45.370
the world. This is the little audio book of Ikigai brought to you by Audible.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.440
Ikigai is a Japanese word for describing the pleasures and meanings of life.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:58.080
The word literally consists of "Iki", to live, and "Gai", reason.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:04.840
So Ikigai is about finding joy in the little things, whether it's sipping a cup of coffee in the morning or

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:10.599
spying a ray of sunshine through the trees, or even just working efficiently at a task.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:14.110
And after you practice this mentality for a little while

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:17.919
you sort of stop looking for external sources of gratification.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:23.140
Which allows you to better focus on and to enjoy the task at hand

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:30.100
Even if it is just work or performing your daily chores. These things actually become enjoyable.

